    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Paul Reynolds are delighted to present to market No. 3 Toragh Glen.\n\nThe property enjoys a wonderful elevated position overlooking the surrounding countryside and Glen Lough, with spectacular panoramic views towards the distinctive silhouette of Muckish Mountain and Downings Beach from the kitchen window.\n\nThe property's large picture windows make the most of this exceptional outlook, bringing the beautiful Donegal landscape directly into the living space.\n\nThe accommodation has a warm and welcoming character, with a bright open-plan living and dining area featuring natural timber flooring, painted timber-panelled ceilings and extensive glazing. The generous reception space provides an ideal setting from which to relax and enjoy the ever-changing views. The modern kitchen is conveniently located adjoining the living area, creating a practical and sociable layout. \n\nExternally, the property benefits from a garden area to the side, providing additional outdoor space and privacy, together with a small timber garden shed. There is also generous gravelled parking to the front and surrounding areas, with mature planting adding to the property's attractive setting.\n\nThe elevated setting provides a wonderful sense of tranquility and offers an exceptional vantage point across the landscape towards Muckish Mountain and the surrounding Donegal countryside.\n\nSituated in the scenic Carrigart area, a mere 8 minutes drive to Downings, this is an appealing property for those looking for a peaceful permanent home, holiday retreat or investment opportunity.\n\nEarly viewing is advised."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway - 5.0 x 1.0\nFloor combination of ceramic tiled and wooden floor.\n\nBedroom 1 - 2.8 x 2.7\nVanity Unit\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.0 x 3.0\nCarpet covering on floor. Suspended timber ceiling.\n\nEnsuite - 3.0 x 2.0\nTiled floor & partially tiled walls. Three piece suite comprising WC, wash hand basin, bath with shower over. Heated towel rail.\n\nOpen plan kitchen/dining/living - 6.4 x 5.7\nSolid wooden floor. Eye and low level units in kitchen. Granite worktop. Suspended timber ceiling with recessed lighting.Steps from living room to dining area. Full length picture with views over Muchish mountian and lake.Door from living area to private raised decking area with coastal views.\n\nBack hall/Utility Room - 2.5 x 1.6\nFloor is a combination of ceramic tile and wooden floor. plumber for washing machine and tumble drier. Suspended timber ceiling.\n\nShower Room - 1.8 x 1.6\nTiled floor and partially tiled walls. Three piece suite comprising wc, wash hand basin and shower.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nCarpet covering on floor. Built in wardrobe. Suspended timber ceiling.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Spectacular elevated views over Glen Lough towards Muckish Mountain </li><li>Views of Downing Beach from kitchen window</li><li>Bright and spacious open-plan living/dining area </li><li>Large picture windows showcasing the panoramic views </li><li>Constructed 1985</li><li>Total floor area 72.81sq mts</li><li>Raised timber decking area to the side of the property</li><li>Stunning views from the decking over Glen Lough towards Muckish Mountain </li><li>Ideal outdoor space for alfresco dining and summer entertaining</li><li>Side garden providing additional outdoor space </li><li>Small timber garden shed for useful storage</li><li>Located within 8 minutes drive from Downings Beach</ul>"
      },
